#! program build/docs-examples/bin/tut21_monitor
#! fresh   /tmp/figure-studio
#! args    --examples /tmp/figure-studio --case /tmp/figure-studio/plate
#! frames  420
#! poster  250
#! crop    0 0 1100 680
#! keys
# F5 runs the plate: the monitor draws the residual on the left axis (log) and the mean temperature on the right one;
# the pointer over it reads the nearest iteration; the left end of the averaging window is dragged right, and the
# window's mean, tagged on the right axis, follows. Input > Boundaries: the sketch of the plate; the pointer on the
# north side draws it thicker; a click on the east side chooses its row in the table
0   wait
0   move 600 300
10  key f5
11  wait
150 move 950 520 15
200 move 820 500 10
215 down
216 move 880 500 20
240 up
265 move 393 33 12
280 down
281 up
295 move 442 106 12
310 down
311 up
330 move 683 100 12
365 move 751 152 10
380 down
381 up
400 move 600 600 15
